{"title":"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Inductive_Reasoning)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Inductive Reasoning)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Integral_Approximation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Integral Approximation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfd7e5a135b0841a7a68690cd7e6b1d887c5e23f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n = \\sin^2(n^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"22\" />. What is the mean of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a10c9ffc55c40fb1d79e2044b58a3b9435833457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1,x_2,x_3,\\dots,x_{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/a/b2a36e0ffd8683e9220398eb16aaa13f19165300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{11}{45} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{22}{45} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{89}{180} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{91}{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"430\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Add up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de563a149a0e500ba7911091d5bbdf7b58a3bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{89}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d9e8047aad2420728c34c39641621fb422d4892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{88}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/476c8ae3be44adf6e65732d0aa219b6ee2bbb569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{90-i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />. Notice\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b7240a2833c84ab1628a99965d3794bbfbd6e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_i+x_{90-i}=\\sin^2(i^{\\circ})+\\sin^2((90-i)^{\\circ})=\\sin^2(i^{\\circ})+\\cos^2(i^{\\circ})=1\\]\" width=\"490\" height=\"20\" />\nby the Pythagorean identity. Since we can pair up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e609f93104b193a2355181ca62ff083ea9fd3821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$89$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> and keep going until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abef9fdb0235b2ede2639538b5bd76711e058fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/d/86d02b9f4fe65d5c9a788a85a28aea71f372c702.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1+x_2+\\dots+x_{90}=44+x_{45}+x_{90}=44+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^2+1^2=\\frac{91}{2}\\]\" width=\"495\" height=\"57\" />\nHence the mean is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fc618ca87dd38867c4be745c675d10ba458b729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{91}{180}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"78\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~kafuu_chino\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can add a term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> into the list, and the total sum of the terms won't be affected since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5ecb16cc84187bc12033307375ad5504cc813d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />. Once <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> is added into the list, the average of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd34ff50f8bba26a08bc96a69e921daa60f5f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> terms is clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Hence the total sum of the terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9d1d3a7b7a18a46e4fb26547771573b341fef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{91}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />. To get the average of the original <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we merely divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a3122c80a6eb7f93e4a14b09cb31f155c4cbadf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{91}{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />. Hence the mean is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fc618ca87dd38867c4be745c675d10ba458b729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{91}{180}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"78\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>This method is called constructing a variable (although most of you already know). \n</p><p>~tsun26, ShortPeopleFartalot\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Inductive_Reasoning.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Inductive_Reasoning)\">Solution 3 (Inductive Reasoning)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Inductive Reasoning)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we use radians to rewrite the question, we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/4748a536c03a6cd7a505ab99d02cf0c7d12bb2a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n=\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{n\\pi}{2\\times90}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"158\" height=\"45\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> have no specialty beyond any other integers, so we can use some inductive processes.\n</p><p>If we change <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/1889ffab39fb8a79ac3fb5a862b724916f6d1a3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)+\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{4}\\right)}{2}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^2+\\left(1\\right)^2}{2}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}+1}{2}=\\frac{3}{4}\\,.\\]\" width=\"398\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>If we change <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f607bdeabf45870c0c46b705d4992d2da304604.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)+\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{6}\\right)+\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{6}\\right)}{3}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(1\\right)^2}{3}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}+1}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{4}{6}\\,.\\]\" width=\"615\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>By intuition, although not rigorous at all, we can guess out the solution if we change <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/0/b00a2058855f4c2f0ac356afafec2b97c5395129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k+1}{2k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"39\" />. Thus, if we plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3e70ece834fb761dc1ed69c5a31547e10643c25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/1290ce346b36c84d9bd2af12f8caf1e8d7da4255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{90+1}{2\\times90}=\\boxed{\\mathbf{(E)}\\,\\frac{91}{180}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"153\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~Prof. Joker\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2024_AMC_12B_P11.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bb/2024_AMC_12B_P11.jpeg/600px-2024_AMC_12B_P11.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"849\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bb/2024_AMC_12B_P11.jpeg/900px-2024_AMC_12B_P11.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/b/bb/2024_AMC_12B_P11.jpeg 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>~Kathan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_2\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d614547172372622e55cb7539734285ddf2b4410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(x) = \\frac{1 - \\cos(2x)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"174\" height=\"40\" />. We want to determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c2c1e4d7f2cbbf6264d3cea8b525040a45fa1c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{90}\\sum_{n = 1}^{90} \\sin^2(n^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"118\" height=\"55\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/7/147ad1e5d503af65ea894f1e43aad11b230498d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} &amp;= \\frac{1}{90} \\sum_{n = 1}^{90} \\frac{1 - \\cos(2n)}{2} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{2} -\\frac{1}{180}\\sum_{n = 1}^{90} \\cos(2n) \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"173\" height=\"110\" />\n</p><p>Graphing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c938e3f9dea789595c6290070f7975f45bc4300a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />, we can pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f1bb3208396a632f4e152367fd8f24e07143232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(2^{\\circ}) + \\cos(178^{\\circ}) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" /> and so on. We are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b785d9581cdfdb3a517409b167a4c5ebc3ec04c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(90^{\\circ}) + \\cos(180^{\\circ}) = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbd81295bf92cfb41934f89504ee539d65bd5ec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{180} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{91}{180}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"169\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~vinyx\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Integral_Approximation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Integral_Approximation)\">Solution 5 (Integral Approximation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Integral Approximation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let \\( f(n) = \\sin^2(n^\\circ) \\)\n</p><p>The function \\( f(n) = \\sin^2(n) \\) is continuous for all real values of \\( n \\). We want to find the average value of \\( f(n) \\) over the interval: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/8/f08efe51a86af9e78cbe3dc87b5d05d691e18368.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left[\\frac{\\pi}{180}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"35\" /> \n</p><p>While there are 90 discrete terms meaning \\( f(n)\\) isn't actually continuous, the interval is very small compared to 90, so calculating the average over EVERY term in the interval will be very close to calculating the average over 90 terms, so we can instead calculate the average value from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90a4e3aed30378b1f3ba33db5336c3928a435b72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"34\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeebb746f8c0d3dac5219c3635617032430afee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p>The average value of \\( f(n) \\) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/7257b04a244794199e1f450c6ba2c2b8ec282cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{180}} \\int_{1\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{180}}^{90\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{180}} \\sin^{2}(x) \\, dx = \\frac{180}{89\\pi} \\int_{\\pi/180}^{\\pi/2} \\sin^2(x) \\, dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"390\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe can solve this integral using the power-reduction identity: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d614547172372622e55cb7539734285ddf2b4410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(x) = \\frac{1 - \\cos(2x)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"174\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b58d5dac2e230dd670373d4220b6a5e29d1739e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{180}{89\\pi} \\int_{\\pi/180}^{\\pi/2} \\frac{1 - \\cos(2x)}{2} \\, dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"203\" height=\"50\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8ac9b08833ae5807bda9c91f3c648ac168139534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{180}{89\\pi} \\left.\\left(\\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{\\sin(2x)}{4}\\right)\\right|_{\\pi/180}^{\\pi/2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"224\" height=\"53\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/334d1f9d1dfc73d8ed2d87bbb3c81ae2343bd1d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{180}{89\\pi} \\left[ \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4} - 0\\right) - \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{360} - \\frac{\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{90}\\right)}{4}\\right) \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"312\" height=\"55\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/732f1b4b4e8062dfb3031c9d862444c3783407fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{180}{89\\pi} \\left( \\frac{89\\pi}{360} + \\frac{\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{90}\\right)}{4} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"204\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe taylor series of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/199e561c062b030d1dd051a5134579594b8200e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\theta) = \\theta - \\frac{\\theta^3}{6} + \\frac{\\theta^5}{120} - \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"223\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/3/7c3f8dfaafef15039eedf8859668ded625ffee80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{90}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"35\" /> is a small angle, we can use a first-order taylor approximation and approximate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b931a954e136830ef581e33b58180c73c7029c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{90}\\right) \\approx \\frac{\\pi}{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Hence, our result is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fceaccd58a181ce563326735bd1f0edfc7d6ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{180}{89\\pi}\\left(\\frac{89\\pi}{360} + \\frac{\\pi}{360}\\right) = \\frac{180}{89\\pi}\\cdot\\frac{90\\pi}{360} = \\frac{180}{89\\pi}\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\frac{45}{89}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"387\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWhile <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4df6867d7a80a4ef9a87551d88cae8851cf5376c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45}{89}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> isn't an option, it is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and out of the given options, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a3122c80a6eb7f93e4a14b09cb31f155c4cbadf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{91}{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> (We approximated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/3/7c3f8dfaafef15039eedf8859668ded625ffee80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{90}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"35\" /> with a first-order taylor approximation and calculated the average value over the interval instead of over 90 discrete values, but it's close enough to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a3122c80a6eb7f93e4a14b09cb31f155c4cbadf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{91}{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />).\n</p><p>So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fc618ca87dd38867c4be745c675d10ba458b729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{91}{180}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"78\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>-sourodeepdeb\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJq7DhLNnZ4&amp;t=0s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gJq7DhLNnZ4&amp;t=0s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B\">2024 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Ans